<title>USA: Weekend U.S. box office chart -- Dec 6-8.</title>
<headline>Weekend U.S. box office chart -- Dec 6-8.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the U.S. box office during the three-day period from December 6 to December 8, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		    Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. 101 Dalmatians	   $13,944,053	 $ 63,690,609</p>
<p>2. Daylight		   $10,014,795	 $ ----</p>
<p>3  Star Trek:</p>
<p>    First Contact	   $ 6,609,903	 $ 71,146,315</p>
<p>4. Jingle All The Way     $ 5,593,605	 $ 38,080,639</p>
<p>5. Ransom		     $ 5,495,131	 $112,913,186</p>
<p>6. Space Jam		  $ 4,540,237	 $ 73,356,183</p>
<p>7. The English Patient    $ 2,707,595	 $ 13,219,641</p>
<p>8. The Mirror Has</p>
<p>    Two Faces		 $ 2,381,388	 $ 37,166,009</p>
<p>9. Set It Off		 $ 1,315,442	 $ 32,366,683</p>
<p>10 Romeo and Juliet	 $ 1,313,651	 $ 41,668,083</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;101&quot; Dalmatians&quot; and &quot;Ransom&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co., &quot;Daylight&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd., &quot;Star Trek: First Contact&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc., &quot;Jingle All The Way&quot; and &quot;William Shakespeare's Romeo and Juliet&quot; are released by News Corp.'s 20th Century Fox. &quot;Space Jam&quot; is released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc., &quot;The English Patient&quot; by Disney's Miramax Films. &quot;The Mirror Has Two Faces&quot; is released Sony Corp. and &quot;Set It Off&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner.</p>
